  "schema:description": "New, ongoing, or resolved diagnoses in biological mother while pregnant (Static Cohort Maternal Information CRF)\nStudy Description\nDescribes the characteristics of HIV-infected pregnant women and their HIV-exposed, uninfected children at clinical sites in Latin America, including the utilization of interventions related to decreasing the risk of mother-to-child transmission. Biospecimens are available for request through DASH. Please navigate to Explore Biospecimens at the top of this page. HIV-infected women and their HIV-exposed uninfected children",
  "schema:distribution": [
    {
      "schema:contentUrl": "https://dash.nichd.nih.gov/dataset/1132",
